	(descr "Stackpole HCS1206FTL500 0.5 mOhm Kelvin shunt R1. Datasheet (rev 5/12/2022) p2 HCS1206...L500: L 3.20+-0.20, W 1.65+-0.20, T 0.90+-0.15, terminal A 0.80+-0.20; p5 1206 land a 1.40 gap, b 1.70, c 1.80. IPC-7351C least density (D109): force land outer edge 1.95 -> 1.75 = L max / 2 + 0.05 (toe 0.15 nominal, 0.05 at L max; terminal inner edge 0.60-1.00 stays on the land, inner gap 1.40 kept); land height 1.80 kept (W max 1.85). Four-pad Kelvin split unchanged: sense pads 2/3 0.40 x 0.40 at x +-0.70..+-1.10, y +0.50..+0.90, 0.10 net-tie gap to the force copper; pads 1/4 force (x +-0.70..+-1.75, y -0.90..+0.90 minus the sense notch). Courtyard 3.70 x 2.00 (was 4.10 x 2.00). The board dissipates 0.2-0.31 W (spec 4.1) into the +BATT pours; the shorter toe reduces the fillet only. Derived from lib:R_1206_Kelvin_4Pad_NetTie_HCS1206_Dense (same frame, pad numbers, 3D model, F.Fab body, no component silk); spec hardware/tools/land_specs/R_1206_Kelvin_4Pad_NetTie_HCS1206_L.json")
